# Cardinal System — Development Rules

Canonical rules: `AGENTS.md` and `AGENTS/*.md`. Do not restate them here.

- Work on `feature/*` | `fix/*` | `chore/*` | `docs/*` from `dev`. PR into `dev`; never commit directly to `dev` or `main`.
- Issue tracking: Dual tracking model (`AGENTS/issues.md`). Integrated Blackboard for runtime agent coordination; GitHub Issues (`enhancement`, `bug`, etc.) mandatory for strict system development. Branches and PRs must reference issues (`Closes #N`).
- Language: English only — docs, skills, comments, identifiers, commits, PRs, prompts. Policy: `AGENTS/docs.md`.
- Commits: Conventional Commits, English subject and body, ≤72 char subject. Details: `skills/cardinal-commit.md`.
- TDD required in auth, keys, ws, db, router.
- Frontend types must match backend JSON 1:1 (flat fields). WS goes to `ws://127.0.0.1:8787/ws`, not the Vite proxy. Use `127.0.0.1`, not `localhost` (cookies).
- Knowledge base: `context/ecosystem.md`. Quirks: `docs/guides/pitfalls.md`. API: `docs/api.md`.

## Cursor as parent

Composer implements 1–2 file changes without critical logic. Delegate otherwise (auth/keys/ws/db/router, multi-file, review, feature docs, verification, another pane/kind).

| Subagent | When |
|----------|------|
| `builder` | Spec in `packages/` (except `ws/`) and `backend/` |
| `ws-protocol` | `packages/ws/**` |
| `frontend` | `frontend/**` |
| `tester` | TDD RED (use proactively in TDD scopes) |
| `verifier` | Someone said done (use proactively) |
| `reviewer` | Diff quality |
| `security-reviewer` | auth/keys/ws/leaks (use proactively) |
| `docs` | Feature already verified |
| `herdr-dispatcher` | Long, parallel, isolation, another kind — only if `HERDR_ENV=1` |

Canonical roles: `docs/agents/roles/`. If this session is the orchestrator (`HERDR_ENV=1` and the human asked): talk to `herdr` directly, kind `cursor`, accept cloud. Otherwise do not spawn Herdr; use `herdr-dispatcher`. OpenCode CLI is optional, not the daily path.
